              h: ['*Jeremiah 51:15 says Jehovah made the earth by his power and the heavens by his understanding.', 'Seraiah threw a scroll tied to a stone into the Euphrates to show Babylon would sink, Jeremiah 51:63, 64.', 'In Jeremiah 52:31-34, King Jehoiachin was let out of prison and ate at the king’s table.', 'Jeremiah 51:46 says not to be afraid of the reports we hear, because Jehovah is in control.'],
              x: ['*At Jeremiah 51:59-64, Seraiah read the scroll in Babylon, tied a stone to it, and threw it into the Euphrates. Revelation 18:21 uses a similar picture of a millstone hurled into the sea. Jehovah’s judgment on false religion will be just as final.', 'Jeremiah 52 ends with Jehoiachin released after 37 years in exile and given a seat above the other kings. Even in captivity, Jehovah kept David’s royal line alive, as he promised at 2 Samuel 7:16. That line would lead to the Messiah.', 'Jeremiah 51:15, 16 contrasts Jehovah, who made the earth and controls the clouds and rain, with idols that verse 17 says have no breath in them. Babylon’s gods could not save her. Our God is the living Creator, so trusting him is never misplaced.', 'Jeremiah 52:17-23 lists the copper pillars and utensils carried off from the temple. The things people felt made the temple safe could not protect it once the nation left Jehovah. What protects us is our relationship with him, not outward symbols.']
