              x: ['*I am grateful for Bible translation. Revelation 14:6 pictures good news going to every nation and tongue, and translating the New World Translation helps make that possible. Our donations help people read God’s Word in the language of their heart.', 'Disaster relief shows practical love. In the first century, the disciples in Antioch sent relief to the brothers in Judea during a famine, Acts 11:28-30. Today, donations let help reach our brothers quickly, and that unity is a powerful witness.', 'I appreciate that donations are pooled so congregations with fewer resources can still have Kingdom Halls and literature. Paul spoke of an equalizing at 2 Corinthians 8:14, where one group’s surplus fills another’s need. No one is left behind.']
